&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;h2&gt;


The Mental Model
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Think of a &lt;strong&gt;printing press with one plate&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Identity:&lt;/strong&gt; the JSX tree is the plate. It is the only original. The HTML you send is a print, and you can make as many prints as you like without redrawing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Update timing:&lt;/strong&gt; Tailwind classes are compiled when you run the press (&lt;code&gt;render()&lt;/code&gt;), not when the app builds. Change a class in the plate and the next print changes; the client never sees the class name.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Read timing:&lt;/strong&gt; clients read only what is physically on the page — inline styles. Anything left in a stylesheet is ink that never touched the paper.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Two consequences follow. First, a class that cannot be inlined (&lt;code&gt;hover:&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;group-hover:&lt;/code&gt;, complex selectors) cannot be trusted, no matter how good it looks in the preview. Second, the pixel preset is not cosmetic: without it, &lt;code&gt;p-6&lt;/code&gt; prints as &lt;code&gt;1.5rem&lt;/code&gt;, and the Word rendering engine behind Outlook desktop does not know what a &lt;code&gt;rem&lt;/code&gt; is.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The template is the plate; the inbox only ever sees the print.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How to Use It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Install React Email. The preview app ships separately.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pnpm add react-email
pnpm add -D @react-email/ui
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;





&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;src/
└── mail/
├── components/
│   ├── email-layout.tsx
│   ├── email-button.tsx
│   ├── email-heading.tsx
│   ├── email-info-card.tsx
│   ├── email-link.tsx
│   └── index.ts
├── templates/
│   ├── welcome-mail.tsx
│   ├── reset-password-mail.tsx
│   └── index.ts
├── mail.types.ts
└── mail-service.tsx
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



