&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuTrigger&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;render&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Button&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;variant&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"secondary"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;size&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"icon-lg"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Sun&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"inline-block dark:hidden"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Moon&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"hidden dark:inline-block"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"sr-only"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Toggle&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuTrigger&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuContent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuGroup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuItem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"light"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Light&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuItem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"dark"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Dark&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuItem&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;onClick&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;setTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"system"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nc"&gt;System&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuItem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuGroup&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenuContent&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DropdownMenu&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;render&lt;/code&gt; prop tells Base UI to use your &lt;code&gt;Button&lt;/code&gt; as the trigger, so keyboard and ARIA behavior stay on a real button. The two icons are plain markup: CSS decides which one is visible from the same &lt;code&gt;.dark&lt;/code&gt; class the boot script set.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now three patterns you can drop into any route.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Put the chooser where people expect it
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeChanger&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/components/theme-changer"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;SiteHeader&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;header&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"flex items-center justify-between border-b px-4 py-3"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"font-medium"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Docs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeChanger&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;header&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;One component offers all three choices, and its icon is already correct on the first frame.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Icons that flip without JavaScript state
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeGlyph&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;aria&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;hidden&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"true"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"inline-block h-4 w-4"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"block h-4 w-4 dark:hidden"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;viewBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"0 0 16 16"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;circle&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cx&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"8"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"8"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;r&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"4"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fill&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"currentColor"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"hidden h-4 w-4 dark:block"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;viewBox&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"0 0 16 16"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;path&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;d&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"M13 10A6 6 0 0 1 6 3a6 6 0 1 0 7 7Z"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;fill&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"currentColor"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;svg&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The &lt;code&gt;dark:&lt;/code&gt; variant reads the same class the boot script set, so the icon is right on the first frame and cannot disagree with hydration.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Show the stored choice, not a guess
&lt;/h3&gt;



&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useTheme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"@/components/providers/theme-provider"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;labels&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;light&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Light"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;dark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Dark"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;system&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"System"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ThemeStatus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useTheme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;className&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"text-sm"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;Theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;labels&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;theme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;span&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Context holds intent, so the label keeps saying "System" even when the OS quietly flips the pixels.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;❌ Do not echo &lt;code&gt;theme&lt;/code&gt; back into storage in an effect: &lt;code&gt;setTheme&lt;/code&gt; already writes it, and a render-time storage read is the bug that broke server rendering in the first place.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When to Use It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Reach for it only when all three are true:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You server-render or prerender, and people can choose light, dark, or system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You control the document shell and can place one inline script before route content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your CSS can key off a class on the root element.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Situation&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Better tool&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Client-only app with no server rendering&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Plain state plus one effect&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Per-card or per-panel themes&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CSS variables scoped to that container&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Theme must be known while generating HTML on server&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Cookie or session value read server-side&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;OS preference is the only option&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark)&lt;/code&gt; in CSS&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Several tabs must stay in sync&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Add a &lt;code&gt;storage&lt;/code&gt; event listener&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;JavaScript needs the resolved mode before first paint&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Publish it as a DOM attribute in the boot script&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Smell test: if your dark mode is decided after the first pixel, you are already debugging a flash.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How It Works Under the Hood
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The context holds intent.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;createContext({ theme: "system", setTheme: () =&amp;gt; {} })&lt;/code&gt; gives &lt;code&gt;useTheme()&lt;/code&gt; a safe default outside a provider. It carries the request, never the painted result, so a &lt;code&gt;system&lt;/code&gt; user stays &lt;code&gt;system&lt;/code&gt; when the OS changes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The boot script paints before hydration.&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;getThemeScript&lt;/code&gt; uses &lt;code&gt;JSON.stringify&lt;/code&gt; for the key and fallback, so developer-supplied strings cannot break the JS literals. It validates the stored value, resolves &lt;code&gt;system&lt;/code&gt; through &lt;code&gt;matchMedia&lt;/code&gt;, and writes a class plus &lt;code&gt;style.colorScheme&lt;/code&gt;; &lt;code&gt;try/catch&lt;/code&gt; degrades blocked storage to the default. It only &lt;em&gt;adds&lt;/em&gt; a class because it runs once on a fresh document, while &lt;code&gt;applyTheme&lt;/code&gt; removes both classes because it can run many times.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Two microtasks replace a render-time read.&lt;/strong&gt; The mount effect reads storage, then queues &lt;code&gt;setCurrentTheme&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;setMounted&lt;/code&gt;; React 19 batches them into one render, so &lt;code&gt;mounted&lt;/code&gt; is never true with the wrong theme. The same read during render would touch &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; on the server.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Effect order handles OS changes.&lt;/strong&gt; The apply effect runs after mount. The listener effect subscribes only while &lt;code&gt;currentTheme === "system"&lt;/code&gt; and cleans up on change, so a fixed theme stops the subscription. An OS flip between boot script and hydration is harmless: the boot class is already right and the mount effect re-applies it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The cost is small but real.&lt;/strong&gt; Every render creates a new context value object and a new &lt;code&gt;setTheme&lt;/code&gt; function; each user choice performs one storage write; each change writes two class operations plus an inline style; a &lt;code&gt;system&lt;/code&gt; user retains one media listener. Memoize consumers if that object identity matters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Phase&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;
&lt;code&gt;currentTheme&lt;/code&gt; in React&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Class on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Decided by&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Server render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;defaultTheme&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;none in markup&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;initial state&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;HTML parse&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;not hydrated&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;dark&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;inline script&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;First paint&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;defaultTheme&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;dark&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;CSS&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Hydration commit&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;defaultTheme&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;dark&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Mount microtask&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;stored &lt;code&gt;dark&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;dark&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;applyTheme&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;OS change while &lt;code&gt;system&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;system&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;flips to &lt;code&gt;light&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;media listener&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Interrupted render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;proposed value, dropped&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;last committed&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;React batching&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server rendering stays clean: DOM APIs live in effects or inside the script &lt;em&gt;string&lt;/em&gt;, never in render, and server and first client render both start at &lt;code&gt;defaultTheme&lt;/code&gt;. If React markup depends on the resolved mode, publish it as a &lt;code&gt;data-theme&lt;/code&gt; attribute in the boot script and read that after mount.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;None of the built-ins solve this. &lt;code&gt;useSyncExternalStore&lt;/code&gt; subscribes to &lt;code&gt;matchMedia&lt;/code&gt; but needs a server snapshot and cannot act before hydration. &lt;code&gt;useLayoutEffect&lt;/code&gt; runs before client paint only and warns during server rendering. React 19's &lt;code&gt;useEffectEvent&lt;/code&gt; stabilizes callback identity, not the first frame. A CSS media query cannot honor a stored choice.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Conclusion
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The trade is a duplicated script in every HTML response in exchange for a correct first frame. You give up the idea that React owns the switch; you gain a page that never shows the wrong theme and a context that stays authoritative for future changes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep intent in context and the painted result on &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;; never mix the two.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate stored values and wrap boot-time storage access in &lt;code&gt;try/catch&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unsubscribe from OS changes as soon as the user picks a fixed theme.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This belongs wherever server-rendered pages offer a theme choice. For a client-only toy with no user preference, a plain CSS media query is the boring answer, and it wins.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a software engineer, I have spent a lot of time this year learning how to build with large language models. The pattern that keeps coming up in real products is not a clever prompt. It is RAG: retrieval-augmented generation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;In simple terms, RAG lets an LLM answer from your data instead of only from what it memorised in training. You store your documents as embeddings, retrieve the most relevant chunks for a question, and give those chunks to the model as context.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It sounds simple. The difference between a demo and a useful product is in the engineering around it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why RAG, and when not to use it
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;RAG is a good fit when:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your answers need to come from private or changing documents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Users ask specific questions, not general knowledge questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You need to show sources, not just an answer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hallucinations are costly, and a wrong answer is worse than no answer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is not the right tool for everything. If the answer is stable, public knowledge, a plain LLM call is faster and cheaper. If you need exact calculations or up-to-date structured data, an API or database query will beat retrieval every time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Choosing RAG is an engineering decision, not a default.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


My stack: FastAPI + Postgres/pgvector + React
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For a practical RAG app, I would keep the stack boring and familiar:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;FastAPI&lt;/strong&gt; for the API, because it is fast to build with in Python and handles async retrieval well&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Postgres with pgvector&lt;/strong&gt; for storage, because you get a real database and vector search in one place, instead of adding a separate vector store too early&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;React with TypeScript&lt;/strong&gt; for the frontend, because the interesting work is in the UI: showing sources, streaming answers, and handling follow-up questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is the same stack I am building with in my current AI upskilling work. Python for the LLM and retrieval logic, React for the product surface.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


The pipeline that actually matters
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A RAG system has four parts, and most failures happen in the first two:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Ingestion:&lt;/strong&gt; Split documents into chunks that make sense on their own. A chunk that cuts a paragraph in half will retrieve badly, no matter how good your model is.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Embedding and storage:&lt;/strong&gt; Store the chunk, its embedding, and its source. Keep the metadata. You will need it to show citations and to debug bad answers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Retrieval:&lt;/strong&gt; Search by meaning, not just keywords. Start with top 5 chunks, then test with real questions. More chunks is not always better, it adds noise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Generation:&lt;/strong&gt; Give the model the retrieved chunks and clear instructions: answer only from the context, say when you do not know, and cite the source.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If an answer is wrong, do not start by changing the model. Check what was retrieved first.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Quality, reliability, and human oversight
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI can accelerate development, but human oversight remains critical here too. A RAG app can retrieve the wrong document, quote it confidently, and look correct.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Good engineering still requires:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Testing with real questions from real users, not just examples that work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measuring retrieval quality, not just whether the final answer sounds good&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logging questions, retrieved chunks, and answers so you can improve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear fallbacks when confidence is low or no relevant document is found&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;RAG does not remove responsibility. It makes the quality of your data and retrieval part of the product.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What I would build first
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you are learning RAG, do not start with a complex agent framework. Build the smallest useful version:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One document set you understand well&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A simple upload and ask flow in React&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;FastAPI endpoints for ingest, ask, and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source citations in every answer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Then iterate on chunking, retrieval, and evaluation. That loop is where the learning happens.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AI is not replacing software engineers. It is reshaping the craft toward system design, data quality, and good judgment about when to trust the model. RAG is a good place to practise exactly those skills, because the model is only as good as the system around it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Hydration errors mean the HTML your server produced differs from what React rendered on the client's first pass. The cause is almost always one of four things: a value that differs between server and browser (dates, locale, random IDs), browser-only APIs read during render, invalid HTML nesting, or a browser extension rewriting the DOM. Find which one it is before reaching for &lt;code&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/code&gt;, because that flag hides the symptom without fixing anything.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What does the error actually say?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Depending on your React and Next.js version (as of late 2026, React 19 with a recent Next.js), you will see one of these in the console:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;Error: Hydration failed because the server rendered HTML didn't match the client.
As a result this tree will be regenerated on the client.

Warning: Text content did not match. Server: "11/25/2026" Client: "25/11/2026"

Warning: Expected server HTML to contain a matching &amp;lt;div&amp;gt; in &amp;lt;p&amp;gt;.
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Newer versions print a diff with &lt;code&gt;+&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;-&lt;/code&gt; lines showing what the client expected versus what the server sent. Read that diff first. It usually points at the exact element, and the element tells you which of the four causes you have.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The cost of ignoring it is real: React discards the server HTML for that tree and re-renders on the client, so you pay for SSR and lose its benefit, and the UI may flicker.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Takeaway: the diff in the console names the mismatching node, and that node tells you the cause.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Which cause do you have?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;div class="table-wrapper-paragraph"&gt;&lt;table&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Symptom in the diff&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Likely cause&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Right fix&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Text differs by date, time, or number format&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;toLocaleString()&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;new Date()&lt;/code&gt; with different timezone or locale on server vs browser&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Render a stable value, format after mount&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Text or &lt;code&gt;id&lt;/code&gt;/&lt;code&gt;key&lt;/code&gt; differs randomly each load&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;Math.random()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Date.now()&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;crypto.randomUUID()&lt;/code&gt; in render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useId()&lt;/code&gt; or generate inside an effect&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Content only exists in the browser&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;window&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;matchMedia&lt;/code&gt; read during render&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;
&lt;code&gt;useSyncExternalStore&lt;/code&gt; or an effect&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;"Expected server HTML to contain a matching &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;"&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Invalid nesting such as &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; inside &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; inside &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Fix the markup&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Extra attributes or nodes you did not write&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Browser extension (translators, dark-mode tools, password managers)&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Test in a clean profile; usually ignore&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Takeaway: four causes cover nearly every hydration error, and each has a different correct fix.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How do I fix dates and locale mismatches?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The server runs in UTC (on most hosts) with its own default locale. The browser uses the user's timezone and language. Any &lt;code&gt;new Date().toLocaleString()&lt;/code&gt; in render will differ.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This breaks:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;PostedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toLocaleString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Two options. If the exact local format does not matter at first paint, pin it so both sides agree:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;PostedAt&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Intl&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nc"&gt;DateTimeFormat&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"en-US"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;dateStyle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"medium"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;timeStyle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"short"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;timeZone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"UTC"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;format&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dateTime&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="no"&gt;UTC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;If you want the viewer's local time, render the stable version first and upgrade after hydration:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"use client"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;LocalTime&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;setText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useState&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toISOString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;slice&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mi"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;16&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;replace&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"T"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;" "&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;" UTC"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;useEffect&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nf"&gt;setText&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;new&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;Date&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;toLocaleString&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;dateTime&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;iso&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;text&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The first client render matches the server, then the effect swaps in the local string. The drawback is a brief visible swap, which is the honest price of showing a per-user value in server-rendered HTML.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Takeaway: either make both sides format identically (pin timezone and locale) or render a stable value and localize in an effect.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


How do I handle random IDs and browser-only values?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For IDs that link labels to inputs, do not invent them yourself. React's &lt;code&gt;useId()&lt;/code&gt; produces values that are stable across server and client:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useId&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;Field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kt"&gt;string&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useId&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;htmlFor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;label&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;/&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;For values that only exist in the browser, such as &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; or a media query, the common mistake is reading them directly during render with a &lt;code&gt;typeof window !== "undefined"&lt;/code&gt; check. That check makes server and client output differ by design, which is exactly the bug. Use &lt;code&gt;useSyncExternalStore&lt;/code&gt;, which takes a separate server snapshot:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"use client"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;useSyncExternalStore&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"react"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;subscribe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;cb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;void&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mq&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;matchMedia&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;mq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;addEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"change"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;mq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;removeEventListener&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"change"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;cb&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="k"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kd"&gt;function&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useIsDark&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nf"&gt;useSyncExternalStore&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;subscribe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nb"&gt;window&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;matchMedia&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;matches&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;// what the server (and first hydration pass) assumes&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;React uses the server snapshot during hydration and then re-renders with the real value if it differs, with no mismatch warning.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A heavier alternative is &lt;code&gt;next/dynamic&lt;/code&gt; with &lt;code&gt;ssr: false&lt;/code&gt; for a component that cannot render on the server at all (a chart library touching &lt;code&gt;window&lt;/code&gt; at import time, say). It works, but that component ships no server HTML, so you lose its content for crawlers and first paint. Use it for widgets, not for content you want indexed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Takeaway: give React a separate server snapshot instead of branching on &lt;code&gt;typeof window&lt;/code&gt; during render.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Why does invalid HTML nesting cause hydration errors?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Browsers repair invalid markup while parsing. If your component renders &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;lt;div&amp;gt;...&amp;lt;/div&amp;gt;&amp;lt;/p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, the HTML parser closes the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; early, so the DOM the browser builds no longer matches the tree React expects. The server output looked fine in your JSX, but the parsed result is different.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Common offenders: a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;ul&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; inside &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; inside another &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;a&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;, a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;tr&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; without &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;tbody&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; context, or a markdown renderer that wraps block components in a paragraph. The fix is to change the markup, for example use &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;span&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; or swap the outer &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;p&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; for a &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;div&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt;. No hydration trick helps here.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Takeaway: if the error mentions an element "in" another element, fix the nesting; no React API can paper over it.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


When is &lt;code&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/code&gt; acceptable?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is a one-level escape hatch for content that is expected to differ and is a single text node or attribute, such as a clock or the &lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;html&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; tag when a theme script sets a class before hydration:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight tsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;html&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;lang&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"en"&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;It does not patch up mismatched structure, and it only applies one level deep. Treat it as a deliberate declaration ("this differs on purpose"), not a way to silence errors you have not diagnosed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Takeaway: use &lt;code&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/code&gt; only for values that are meant to differ, never for unexplained errors.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Is it a browser extension?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before debugging your code for an hour, open the page in a private window with extensions disabled, or a fresh browser profile. Translators, dark-mode injectors, and some password managers add attributes or wrap text nodes, producing mismatches that exist only on your machine. If the error vanishes in a clean profile, your app is fine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


FAQ
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why does the hydration error only happen in production or only on refresh?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Production often runs the server in a different timezone and locale than your laptop, and caches rendered HTML, so date and locale mismatches appear only there. Also check whether a value is read from cookies or &lt;code&gt;localStorage&lt;/code&gt; that differs between first and later visits.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Does a hydration error break my Next.js app?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
React recovers by discarding the server HTML for the affected tree and rendering it on the client, so the page usually works but you lose SSR benefits for it and may see flicker. Treat it as a real bug, not cosmetic noise.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Can I just use &lt;code&gt;useEffect&lt;/code&gt; to fix every hydration mismatch?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Only for value mismatches such as dates or browser-only data. It cannot fix invalid HTML nesting, which must be corrected in the markup.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


Bottom line
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Read the diff, classify the mismatch, and apply the matching fix: stable formatting or an effect for dates, &lt;code&gt;useId&lt;/code&gt; for IDs, &lt;code&gt;useSyncExternalStore&lt;/code&gt; for browser state, corrected markup for nesting. Keep &lt;code&gt;suppressHydrationWarning&lt;/code&gt; for values that are meant to differ. If you keep hitting these across a large codebase, a lint rule banning &lt;code&gt;Date.now()&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Math.random()&lt;/code&gt; in render is cheaper than debugging each one.&lt;/p&gt;

